Recent questions: Draw a square in TikZ 
Recent assistant focus: Type to start learning. | Here's a simple TikZ drawing of a square:

```tikz
\documentclass[tikz,border=3.14mm]{standalone}
\usetikzlibrary{positioning, calc, angles, quotes}
\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}
    \coordinate (A) at (0,0);
    \coordinate (B) at (2,0);
    \coordinate (C) at (2,2);
    \coordinate (D) at (0,2);

    \draw (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- (D) -- cycle;

    \node[below left] at (A) {A};
    \node[below right] at (B) {B};
    \node[above right] at (C) {C};
    \node[above left] at (D) {D};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}
```

This code creates a square with vertices labeled A, B, C, and D. The square has side length 2 units. You can adjust the coordinates to change the size or position of the square.

